  "method": {
    "window": "Merged PRs (merged on/after 2025-09-25), walked newest-merged first. Because these projects are very active, the walk only reached the most recent days/weeks before the per-repo cap was hit (see merged_date_range_examined).",
    "stopping_rule": "Stopped each repository after the 3rd qualifying PR (self-imposed cap of 3 to spread the 30 PRs over 10 repos; the task allowed up to 4). The last PR examined in each repo is therefore always a qualifying one, which biases the per-repo rate upward, especially for repos where the cap was hit quickly.",
    "examined": "Every PR in the range was looked at in listing form. Single-commit PRs cannot show an in-PR fix (force-pushes/squashes are invisible), so they were counted as examined but not inspected further. Every multi-commit non-bot PR had its non-merge commits checked; any commit that looked like a fix was opened (diff, review comments).",
    "bot_or_automated": "Renovate/Dependabot/Crowdin/translation-sync PRs and automated release PRs; counted in prs_examined but reported separately.",
    "one_bug_per_pr": "When a PR contained several in-PR bug fixes, the entry records the FIRST commit that fixes a bug introduced earlier in the PR (lint/type-only/test-refactor commits and pure design changes skipped); later ones are mentioned in the entry's notes.",
    "sha_source": "All SHAs copied from gh API output. For some PRs the review comment refers to a pre-rebase commit that no longer appears in the PR commit list; buggy_sha then names the surviving commit that introduced the code."
  },
